%S A365082 3,9,11,17,19,25,27,41,43,49,59,67,73,81,83,89,97,107,113,121,131,137,
%T A365082 139,163,169,179,193,211,227,233,241,243,251,257,281,283,289,307,313,
%U A365082 331,337,347,353,361,379,401,409,419,433,443,449,457,467,491,499,521,523,529
%N A365082 Prime powers (A246655) q such that -2 is a nonzero square in the finite field F_q.
%C A365082 Prime powers q that are congruent to 1 or 3 modulo 8 (see A366526).
%C A365082 Odd prime powers q such that (-2)^((q-1)/2) = 1 in F_q.
%C A365082 Prime powers q such that x^2 + 2 splits into different linear factors in F_q[x].
%C A365082 Union of {p^r : p == 1, 3 (mod 8) prime, r >= 1} and {p^r : p == 5, 7 (mod 8) prime, r >= 2 even}.
%C A365082 By Hensel's lemma, also prime powers q such that -2 is a square in Q_q, where Q_{p^f} is the unique degree-f unramified extension of the p-adic field Q_p. See A085759 for a more general statement. - _Jianing Song_, Nov 24 2026
%H A365082 Jianing Song, <a href="/A365082/b365082.txt">Table of n, a(n) for n = 1..10000</a>
%H A365082 Wikipedia, <a href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Hensel%27s_lemma">Hensel's lemma</a>.
%e A365082 49 is a term since -2 = -9 = (+-3i)^2 in F_49 = F_7(i).
%t A365082 Select[Range[600], MemberQ[{1, 3}, Mod[#, 8]] && PrimePowerQ[#] &] (* _Amiram Eldar_, Mar 19 2026 *)
%o A365082 (PARI) isA365082(n) = isprimepower(n) && (n%8==1 || n%8==3)
%Y A365082 Supersequence of A033200.
%Y A365082 Cf. A246655. See A085759 for related sequences.
